# The known failures of h2spec 2.6.0 against examples/httpx/stress_h2.bend
# in the mode ok, as read from the JUnit report: one line per test, in the
# form "<package> | <test case>". A line that passes today prints "now
# passing" and does not fail the gate. A failure with no line here fails
# the gate.
#
# Use the official h2spec 2.6.0 release. A binary built from the same
# commit with a newer Go shows 7 failures a more (task-073 records the
# measure).
#
# 4.2.3: the module announces MAX_FRAME_SIZE 65535, so a 20 KiB HEADERS
# frame is legal. The limit is fixed by tests/io/http2_frame_over.bend.
#
# 5.1.2.1 left this list in task-072: the buffered form reads a chunk,
# admits every HEADERS of the chunk before it answers one, and holds a
# stream open while its answer waits. tests/io/http2_pq_batch.bend fixes
# the wire.
http2/4.2 | Sends a large size HEADERS frame that exceeds the SETTINGS_MAX_FRAME_SIZE
